  "findings": [
    "Changing classification resolution reduces complete checked recovery from 13 to 12, so do not globally replace the coarse targets.",
    "The masks differ by only 0.699375% on rabbit, yet the selected slit counts change from 3/3 to 3/4 and its main shape deteriorates. Cross-scoring establishes a much better original-target fit already exists; this is not simply an impossible sharper target.",
    "On rabbit, the finer mask adds a 61-pixel isolated border region. The early feature initializer skips that border region and no weak-interior-region proposal runs. A controlled perturbation is needed to isolate the scheduling effect.",
    "Both targets retain the same source observations, including the star pixels beyond the photograph. No padding contributes to scores.",
    "All 25 accepted outputs pass editable validation. Rabbit and bicycle crop-RGB candidates fail editor geometry conversion and were already rejected by engine checks; the controller remains failed at that audit."
  ],
  "nextStep": "Isolate the rabbit border fragment and weak-region scheduling without weakening final feature gates. Evaluate image noise and printed-paper identity separately from path fitting.",
